{%- comment -%}
  PG Page Wide: full-width page, centred Contact card.

  pg-page-style caps and centres EVERY direct child of #content:

      html body #content > *{ max-width:1000px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto }
      html body #content   { padding:52px 20px 76px !important }

  That single rule does two jobs at once, which is why the first two attempts
  here traded one problem for the other. Lifting the cap freed the banners and
  let the form stretch to the full viewport. Restoring a cap on `> *` reined in
  the form and squeezed the banners back down with it.

  So the two are separated. The cap comes off `> *` entirely -- anything
  full-bleed stays full-bleed -- and is re-applied only to the pieces that make
  up the contact panel itself: the form card and the heading above it. Both get
  the same width and the same auto margins, so they sit in one centred column
  on a page that is otherwise the full width of the screen.

  SPECIFICITY. pg-page-style is 21st in footer-group and this renders from
  pg-cart-fast, which is 4th, so on equal specificity pg-page-style wins every
  tie. Its `max-width:1000px` carries no !important and is beaten outright, but
  its heading and padding rules do, and they are written at `html body #content
  ...`. The doubled id here (`#content#content`) buys the point that decides it
  regardless of load order.

  MOBILE IS UNTOUCHED. pg-page-style narrows the gutters to 14px under 600px
  and that is what keeps the form usable on a phone; the padding change here is
  inside min-width:601px, and a 1100px cap is far wider than any phone.

  Gated on the page handle in Liquid, exactly as pg-page-style is.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pgw_h = page.handle | default: '' -%}
{%- if pgw_h == 'contact' or pgw_h == 'track-order' or pgw_h == 'track-your-order' -%}
<style>
  /* the page itself: no cap, so anything full-bleed stays full-bleed */
  html body #content#content > *{max-width:none !important}

  /* the contact panel: one centred column, card and heading aligned to it */
  html body #content#content form[action*='contact'],
  html body #content#content .pgp-card,
  html body #content#content h1,
  html body #content#content .pgp-title{
    max-width:1100px !important;
    margin-left:auto !important;
    margin-right:auto !important;
    width:100% !important;
    box-sizing:border-box !important;
  }

  @media (min-width:601px){
    html body #content#content{
      padding-left:clamp(20px,4vw,72px) !important;
      padding-right:clamp(20px,4vw,72px) !important;
    }
  }
</style>
{%- endif -%}
